speechtext:
The first schedule reads:
1.	Capital employed at beginning of period.- For the purposes of this act, capital employed in any year or fiscal period means the capital at the beginning of the said period computed in the manner hereinafter specified.
2.	Capital includes.-Capital shall be taken to be the following, subject to the deductions hereinafter provided:
(a)	Cost of assets.-So far as it consists of assets acquired by purchase on or after the commencement of the business, the price at which those assets were acquired and where the price of any asset has been satisfied otherwise than in cash, the then value of the consideration actually given for the asset shall be treated as the price at which the said asset was acquired;
(b)	Accounts receivable less reserve for bad debts.-So far as it consists of assets being debts due to the person carrying on the business, the full amount of those debts subject to any deduction which has been allowed under the Income War Tax Act in respect thereof on account of bad debts;
(c)	Value of assets acquired otherwise than by purchase.-So far as it consists of any other assets which have been acquired otherwise than by purchase as aforesaid, the value of the assets when they became assets of the business;
(d)	Amount of money and bank deposits.- The amount of money or bank deposits which are actually used by the taxpayer in the business.
Then there are the deductions.
